# ⚽ Panini FIFA World Cup 2026 – Sticker Tracker

A single-file, offline-first HTML sticker tracker for the official **Panini FIFA World Cup 2026** sticker album. No app, no account, no internet required — just open the file in any browser and start ticking.

---

## Features

- **All 992 stickers tracked** — 48 teams × 20 stickers, 20 introduction foil stickers, and 12 Coca-Cola bonus stickers
- **Foil stickers** — team badges (sticker 1) and all FWC intro stickers animate with a sweeping silver shimmer; the shimmer continues in silver when ticked
- **Completed team celebration** — finish a team and its header turns solid medal gold with a gentle glow
- **Hover colours** — green glow for incomplete teams, gold glow for completed ones
- **Coca-Cola section** — 12 bonus sticker slots styled in Coca-Cola red, found under bottle labels
- **Persistent progress** — ticks are saved automatically in browser `localStorage`; no button required
- **Export Progress** — bakes your current ticks into a new copy of the HTML file so you can move your collection between devices without losing anything
- **Smart reset** — Reset All clears everything without the baked data bouncing straight back
- **Filter buttons** — view All / Incomplete Only / Complete Sets / Not Started
- **Fully offline** — one self-contained `.html` file, no dependencies, no CDN calls
- **Built-in FAQ** — collapsible how-to guide inside the file for anyone who downloads it

---

## How to Use

1. **Download** `World_Cup_2026_Sticker_Tracker.html`
2. **Double-click** the file to open it in your browser
3. **Tick** any sticker box you own — it saves instantly
4. Use **↓ Export Progress** to download a copy with your ticks baked in for sharing or moving to another device

> If you downloaded from Reddit or a zip archive, make sure to **save the file first**, then open it — don't preview it inside the archive.

---

## Moving Between Devices

Progress is stored in your browser's `localStorage`, which is device- and browser-specific. To move your collection:

1. Click **↓ Export Progress** — downloads a new HTML file with your ticks embedded in the source
2. Send it to your other device (email, WhatsApp, AirDrop, etc.)
3. Open it there — all your ticks are already present
4. Repeat whenever you collect more stickers

